<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <ResourcePreloader />

    @* Lora for headings, Atkinson Hyperlegible for body — the latter was designed for
       low-vision readability, which suits a puzzle people squint at. Both have local
       fallbacks in app.css if the fonts fail to load.

       Lora replaced Fraunces (2026-09-10). Fraunces' "wonk" letterforms — notably an
       f that drops a hooked tail below the baseline — read as a typo at masthead size.
       That is a real axis in the typeface, but Google Fonts ships it as separate static
       files rather than a variable axis, so font-variation-settings can't switch it off.
       Lora carries the same editorial weight without the quirk, and being closer to
       Georgia it degrades better when the webfont fails. *@
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Atkinson+Hyperlegible:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Lora:wght@400..700&display=swap" />

    @* Bootstrap was removed: nothing in the markup used a Bootstrap class (every
       class is oad-* prefixed), and its reboot fought the design system in app.css. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["OneADay.styles.css"]" />
    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</head>

<body>
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
    <ReconnectModal />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    <script src="@Assets["js/confetti.js"]"></script>
    <script src="@Assets["js/twentyfour.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
